1. Scope and grant

Good Morning Technology, LLC ("GM Wallet") offers this license for the code
and documentation it owns or is authorized to license in the release that
includes this notice (the "Software"). Separately licensed material,
including third-party dependencies and components with their own license
notices, remains subject to its respective license.

Subject to the conditions below, GM Wallet grants each recipient a
worldwide, non-exclusive, royalty-free license to use, run, copy, study,
modify and distribute the Software and works derived from it. Commercial
use is included, subject to section 2.

2. Company revenue and paid licensing

A company whose annual group revenue strictly exceeds USD 1,000,000 must
obtain a separate paid written license from GM Wallet before using the
Software or exercising any other permission under this license. This also
applies to use on the company's behalf, including by employees and
contractors, whether for internal operations, hosting or customer-facing
services. A company that crosses the threshold during use must obtain the
paid license before continuing. At exactly USD 1,000,000, a company remains
eligible for this community license.

Annual group revenue means the combined worldwide revenue from all business
activities of the company and its affiliates over the immediately preceding
twelve months. An affiliate is an entity that directly or indirectly
controls, is controlled by, or is under common control with the company.
Control means the power to direct an entity's management or policies
through voting rights, contract or otherwise. Count each entity once,
eliminate transactions within the group, and include revenue for the
portion of the period during which each entity belonged to the group. A
newly formed entity counts its actual revenue for that period.

Use revenue recognized under applicable accounting standards before
deducting costs or expenses. The threshold applies regardless of the profit
or loss of the company or group. Amounts processed for others count only to
the extent recognized as the group's own revenue. Convert non-USD revenue
using a consistently applied published exchange rate applicable to the
period in which the revenue was recognized.

3. Distribution and corresponding source

If you distribute the Software or a work derived from it, retain its
copyright, attribution and license notices, provide a copy of this license,
and prominently identify changes you made and their dates. License the
entire derived work to recipients under this same license. Independent
works merely distributed alongside the Software keep their own licenses.
Each distributor grants recipients the permissions in section 1 for its own
contributions. Each recipient receives those permissions directly from the
relevant copyright holders, subject to that recipient's eligibility under
section 2. You may charge for copies or services. You may not impose
additional restrictions on the permissions granted to recipients by this
license.

When distributing a binary, executable or container image, give each
recipient the complete corresponding source for that exact version, either
with the copy or through a clearly identified download available at no
additional charge for as long as you distribute that version. Corresponding
source means the preferred form for making changes, including your
modifications and the scripts and configuration templates needed to build,
install and run the distributed version. It excludes ordinary system tools
and libraries that are generally available and used unmodified. Private use
or operating a network service, by itself, does not trigger this
distribution obligation. Section 2 still applies.

4. Termination and rights reserved

If you breach these terms, your permissions under this license terminate.
Termination does not affect the rights of recipients who independently
